<div id="S3.Thmtheorem34" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem34.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.34</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem34.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem34.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is another important positive integer <math id="S3.Thmtheorem34.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{k}\in\mathbf{Z}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{k}\in\mathbf{Z}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is closely related to <math id="S3.Thmtheorem34.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Waldhausen in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wal82</a>]</cite> more generally discussed a homotopy commutative square where the columns are fibration sequences</p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
